What is and is not redistributed
--------------------------------

This repository indexes the registry: package ids, versions, authors, tags, function
names, the descriptions written by each package author, and a URL to the package.

It does NOT redistribute the DAX code (`functions.tmdl`). That stays at the registry,
where it is kept current. See docs/decisions/2026-08-10-dax-lib-catalog-only.md for
why.

Per-package licensing
---------------------

The upstream repository carries a single MIT license naming SQLBI, but its packages
come from roughly 40 different authors and the package manifest schema has no license
field at all — there is no per-package declaration and no stated contribution policy.
The usual reading is that a contribution to an MIT repository is offered under that
MIT, but it is a convention here, not a documented agreement.

Anyone reusing a package's code in a product should check that package upstream first.

